    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d20">

                <pb facs="0029" n="15" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg15"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710 Consultation (3)A/746b: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Ambassador in Uruguay</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-08T20:00:00-04:00">June 8, 1944—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>330. For Sanders from Knapp. Press statement issued by Department June 6<anchor
                        n="53" xml:id="d20-f1"/>, the date agreed upon for Ecuadoran
                        recognition<anchor n="54" xml:id="d20-f2"/> by most republics, stated that
                    our decision followed after consultations <pb facs="0030" n="16" xml:id="pg16"/>
                    among the republics concerned, in compliance with Resolution XXII, and that we
                    were informing the Committee of our decision. Please so advise Dr. Guani. You
                    may also inform him that we authorized suggestions to the other countries that
                    they notify the Committee of their action, which some have already indicated
                    they propose to do. [Knapp.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d20-f1" n="53" xml:id="d20-f1-content">
                <p>Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, June 10, 1944, p.
                    536.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d20-f2" n="54" xml:id="d20-f2-content">
                <p>For correspondence on the recognition of the new Government in Ecuador by the
                    United States, see <ref target="#pg1036">pp. 1036</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
